  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything. Removing `channel` from `OrderPlaced` conflicts with ARCH-4 in `CLAUDE.md`.\n\n- **The event:** billing-service and analytics-ingest consume `OrderPlaced`, and ARCH-4 says changes must be additive. Removals have to go through deprecation. \"Nothing reads channel anymore\" may well be true, but I can't check it from this repo, and a deployed consumer that validates or requires the field would break.\n- **The order model:** `channel` is also in `src/core/order.ts`, and it's a required, validated input on `POST /orders` (`requestParsing.ts`). Dropping it from the model means changing that API contract. I haven't checked whether the `GET /orders/{id}` response includes it, but if it does, ARCH-8 applies because web-storefront uses that endpoint.\n\nHere is a way to do it safely:\n1. Stop requiring `channel` on `POST /orders` and ignore it if it's sent. Remove it from the order model and the validation. This is safe for clients, as long as the `GET` responses don't expose it.\n2. Mark `channel` as deprecated on `OrderPlaced` (a comment or changelog note) and announce it to the billing-service and analytics-ingest owners. Keep emitting it, which means a fixed placeholder value once the model no longer stores it. Remove it from the event after they confirm they don't read it and have deployed.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n- **(a)** Do step 1 now, with the event still carrying a deprecated `channel`.\n- **(b)** Remove it everywhere now. If so, please confirm that both consumer teams have signed off and that web-storefront doesn't read `channel` from `GET /orders/{id}`.",
